module gunbc.plans.logical_work_realization

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import std.types { List }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn logical_work_realization_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "**Goal:** callers state logical work and irreducible inputs; existing fabric owns storage placement/access/prerequisites, and existing completion/selection/materialization authorities own their respective routes. Pure computation, observation, durable mutation and fresh effects retain distinct identity, freshness, ordering and retry laws: common authoring does not make mutation memoizable. Proposal only; no implicit-operand implementation, runtime-policy change or deployment authorization."),
    p(text: "**Pilot:** keep source_snapshot_handoff() as the no-argument external entry. Replace concrete file-root operands throughout fabric_source_snapshot capture/materialization with one FabricStorageBinding selected at the existing fabric/deployment root. capture_source_snapshot takes store, SourceComposition and inclusions; materialize_source_snapshot takes store, manifest, ProviderWorkspace and expected composition. Preserve local workspace semantics, child-before-parent/manifest publication, exact-preimage/content checks and the actual child-process control. Do not claim cryptographic identity: fabric_object_identity_is_a_structural_locator remains the frontier. Heads, claim enumeration, general inference and production metering are not prerequisites for this object-only slice."),
    p(text: "**Policy:** inherit existing scoped SLO requirements and arbitration authority by module/symbol, not copied credentials/provider/path facts or a new profile algebra. A required unknown remains unresolved; an explicit no-extra-performance-target adds no promise. A departure belongs at the requirement’s owning scope and cannot weaken mandatory consistency/durability/retention/sharing/access/effect contracts. SLOs name subject, operation/workload, metric/units, bound, population/window, evidence and consequence. Costs include relevant setup/transfer/migration; unknown never means zero."),
    p(text: "**Example selection:** one fixed object put/readback workload supplies local 0 micro-USD/0 ms and R2 1/1 as example predictions, not prices or measurements or whole-snapshot cost. Preserve standing in SelectionReceipt using existing CostAxisPredicted/CostTimePredicted/CitedFigureStanding where appropriate. With both admissible, local wins; in a second isolated context, an explicit sharing/reachability requirement excludes the HOST-LOCAL candidate and admitted R2 executes. File-backed served storage can itself be shared; name the actual scope. Changing supplied evidence must change a feasible winner where appropriate. Required physical SLO floors still need admissible evidence (SelectionNeedsEvidence); unresolved alternatives need policy (SelectionNeedsPolicy). Use select_realization/std.pareto/ValuedObjective; UniqueSurvivorRequired or PreferSurvivor cannot select an infeasible candidate or encode list order."),
    p(text: "**Continuity:** preserve an allocated mutable resource’s authority across calls/restarts. Unavailable authority refuses; it never means empty or a new fallback store. Fresh isolated resources may select another admitted backend; existing-state movement is a separately admitted, costed transition. Immutable-result reuse remains with materialization_ladder/provider, which exclude mutable keyed state. Observed domain I/O refusal/contention is a runtime outcome; a missing derivation carries its dependency path/addressee. Preserve lower-level lost-race/readback reasons currently flattened by WorktreeClaimNotRecorded rather than mint a rival taxonomy."),
    p(text: "**Existing storage homes:** std.fabric_storage owns object/head/closure contracts; fabric_storage_client owns FabricStorageBinding and common operations; fabric_storage_file_store, fabric_object_r2 and fabric_storage_r2_head own realizations. Carry existing FabricObjectGet/file_get/R2 get through the binding and served codecs; no head publication merely to read an object. R2 was not a binding arm in the audit. Before adapting callers, model operation capability, uncertain publication and custody at those existing homes. Unsupported head/closure operations are excluded before ranking and direct unsupported calls refuse. R2 PutIfAbsent/PutIfMatch and R2HeadCasAdmitted remain prerequisites; publish objects before heads and preserve conflict/history/unknown-write semantics."),
    p(text: "**Access and identity:** placement/binding retains the shared store’s admitted socket/HTTPS door and protected /state signatures/private root. Host-local stores such as compute_capacity_store retain their separately admitted scope; zero example cost grants no bypass. Extend fabric_state_operation, protocol/wire/state-auth/serve paths together for served get; malformed replies and unknown operations refuse. R2 uses its allocation/purpose/directional-credential and staging-transfer/cleanup authorities, never a fabricated tailnet identity or a second credential route. Configuration resolution (FabricBlobTargetReady) is not readiness evidence."),
    p(text: "**Readiness:** type selected-provider product goals/evidence in fabric/domain before consumers. Use EnsurePolicy/EnsureObservation/ensure_observation_as_attempt with inspect_goal/assess_by_deviations_and_unknowns. ObserveOnly assesses; authorized roots may ensure/apply then independently read back. Observer is goal-blind; malformed/mismatched subjects give GoalAssessmentRefused, deviations/unknowns remain typed, and observation refusal is outside assessment. GoalSatisfied needs every actual component observation; generic classification proves neither population completeness nor execution. Only selected-provider prerequisites apply. Ordinary data users gain no bucket-admin/bootstrap authority."),
    p(text: "**Readiness defects to close:** fabric_storage_file_root_ensure currently treats successful Mkdir.Parents as Ready without owner/mode/readback. Repair through owned_directory_ensure independently of R2/selection, including derived capacity/objects/heads consumed by compute_reserve_against→compute_seat, prepare_snapshot_workspace and fabric_event_log_probe. This is source evidence of control_plane_acknowledgement_minted_as_effect, not a claimed permissions incident. R2 ensure_r2_purpose_bucket/purpose/create needs reusable actual bucket/allocation/credential evidence and ObserveOnly policy; its line/held outcome is not that evidence. FabricWorkspace is the pilot purpose, but empty desired lifecycle rules currently skip lifecycle observation; establish absence of deletion rules before admitting durable domains that depend on it."),
    p(text: "**Selection-to-use frontier:** selected binding must be the actual put/get operand and readiness/use must derive from the same values. Existing ensure plus executed independent readback closes the pilot; ConvergedEffect over supplied reports cannot prove execution. Shared SelectionReceipt→admission→actuation→observation remains std.goal_assessment’s fleet_converge_plan frontier (generation, held lease, observed baseline, CAS), not a competing generic loop. Changing subject/candidates/constraints/policy/evidence invalidates selection; response cannot retroactively prove prior admission. Keep goals corpus-declared because goal revision is not modeled; a runtime-changing profile would introduce stale readiness. General omitted operands remain compiler-architecture/ensure-closure work, not a handwritten setup registry."),
    p(text: "**Claim delivery:** record/read/update/enumerate/settle is one complete consumer after its missing fabric contracts land. worktree_claim_record_before_add(root,claim) is replaced, not overloaded with a second logical operation; the desired claim-only call remains an inference target. The directory stores ownership records, not checkouts. Trace worktree_claim_open→attempt_open_payload→file_compare_and_set before replacement; head-only/windowed CAS is not interchangeable with unwindowed lifecycle storage. FabricClosureRead from one head is not cas_slot_keys enumeration. Establish namespace, complete recovery, retention, consistency and continuity before admitting any backend for claims."),
    p(text: "**Claim invariants:** preserve reference/deadline/generation/codec/admit_callers checks, terminal reasons and existing retained history. Record plus identity/path readback precedes git worktree add. Session settlement and activation reconciliation precede claim cleanup; settlement precedes new acquisition. Keep live/dirty/unpushed/capture-pending/foreign/uncertain trees; remove only admitted trees, observe absence, then expected-generation close. Lost close race never releases ownership. Enumeration failure fails the pass; recover claims left before checkout creation, never infer them from checkout directories. Moving metadata does not move worktrees, credential/runtime files, capacity ledgers or host cleanup authority."),
    p(text: "**Complete claim cut:** roadmap_attempt_worktree_claim’s read/open/close/record_before_add/close_recorded/ensure_one/ensure_pass_at and both roadmap_belt_actuate entrances (belt_worktree_claim_before_add, belt_worktree_claim_ensure) migrate together; internal helpers may retire when obligations survive at the root. Preserve claim codec and lifecycle confined writer references. Wet entrances are open_claim, pass and a_git_that_could_not_run_is_red_and_keeps_the_tree; remove the unused worktree_claim_open import rather than count it as a caller. worktree_claim_slots_root/of/directory and dashboard_instance_directory_demands enrollment disappear only after fabric readiness owns both setup/use. Derive dashboard provisioning, live_deploy spec/emission/readback and runner_host_grants from the SAME requirements; preserve unrelated directories, access admission and failure ordering."),
    p(text: "**Runtime/deployment scopes:** preserve belt_instance_obligation_run→belt_run_once_cli_in→belt_run_once_in→belt_tick_for_instance, selected through GUNBC_BELT_SPAWN_WORKDIR/dashboard_instance_for_repo_root; convenience entry functions do not prove another route executed. Cover dashboard root-ensure/macbook/srv2/lab entrypoints and live_deploy desired/prod-role/operator/transaction routes. srv1 production’s DispatchStateHostShared /opt/gunbc/attempt-state/worktree-claims differs from lab and srv2 instance-owned roots; node_id+attempt_key alone omits that namespace. Preserve Linux service and macOS briansrls:staff ownership. External/supplied deployments and actual rollout revisions require owners’ inventory beyond public built-ins."),
    p(text: "**Existing-state transition:** C1 must name source namespaces/consumers, fence writers and recovery, represent/reconcile records and required generations independently, then perform one authority switch. Preparation failure retains old authority; after new writes, returning to an old snapshot is NOT rollback and needs its own continuity proof. Recovery reads current claims; that does not itself require full-history traversal, but unwindowed retained data cannot disappear incidentally. Name retention/audit compatibility before choosing representation; cas-slot- prefix does not encode prior host/instance namespace. No authorization here to stop services or copy private state."),
    p(text: "**Staffing/order:** R1 repairs file readiness; R2 supplies typed R2 prerequisites; one F integrator owns shared model/binding/codecs/direct outcomes together; S then owns snapshot through child-process result. One C1/C2 owner specifies and executes the full claim cut with fabric/deployment review. Split work only at settled contracts. Credential/session-placement stores and approval simplification are later cohorts, not pilot prerequisites. A modeling package may expose an unresolved contract; do not label it implementation-ready."),
    p(text: "**Compatibility, not automatic migration:** changing FabricPut/HeadAdvance/ObjectGet requires all constructors, eliminators, codecs, forwarders and transitive event-log/CAS consumers to handle new outcomes in that delivery. Unknown object publication/custody is not absence/success/definite failure; if this attempt never advanced a head, do not label its own head update unknown merely because another writer could advance. Preserve checkpoint object+head composition, request-bound workspace_commit_classify and coverage advancement; its object half cannot move while its head remains elsewhere. R2 identity projections cannot reuse LocalFiles’ unproxied explanation. Keep default fabric_state_storage_binding mutable authority unchanged during the object pilot."),
    p(text: "**Census instrument/scope:** rederive tracked actual calls/constructor matches, excluding definitions/imports/comments/quoted prose and pure hold-plan helpers, then inspect enclosing declarations. Subjects: durable_cas_file_store I/O (generation read/probe/window/retained/observe/verify/commit/reclaim/compare-and-set/keys), durable_exclusive_hold_file_store observed acquire/release/recovery, attempt_lifecycle read/commit/advance/open/begin-launch/terminate, durable_cas_fabric_storage observe/head/CAS, plus FabricStorageBinding/Put/HeadAdvance/ObjectGet constructors and operation/result readers. Separate tests/instruments from production; counts overlap and are never a migration gate. The [2026-10-22 census at 7be4375e5a19, exact selectors and direct-site rosters](https://github.com/gunb-ai/gunbc/blob/06d3c1c3149a7420c4a548b9aba9b15c721c635d/dag/gunbc/plans/logical_work_realization.dag) retain the source snapshot. It proves neither compile reachability, deployment, external/private callers, dynamic entry names nor all filesystem I/O; the refresh-and-disposition requirement is retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling (`gunbc.design_ruling bad_process_is_worse_than_no_process`), which establishes no coverage of those callers."),
    p(text: "**Cohort obligations:** immediate lifecycle compatibility includes work_provider_local, compute_seat_ensure, dispatch_credential_acquisition, claims, session_activation_ensure and session_placement. Credential metadata remains distinct from secret/runtime custody and recovery’s local instance root; preserve durable registration before snapshot/launch, confidential readers and tombstones. Placement preserves slot-before-capacity, rollback-only activation, settlement-before-acquisition and no release on lost close race. Approval stores preserve replay/monotonic/single-use/revocation/pending enumeration; approval_store_receipt reads generation 1 after asker authentication, so latest-only replacement is invalid. Commissioning preserves admission/phase order/provenance; printed_chassis.assembly_inventory_store preserves generation fencing and independent capture before actuation."),
    p(text: "**Separate contracts:** existing workspace allocation/gateway/acquisition/release/milestones/metrics and tailnet-door fabric CAS need result compatibility, not backend migration. File-hold providers/readers (fabric cell/control/build allocation, printer, host-unit, intake, commissioning/workspace) retain exclusion, owner/generation fencing, liveness/recovery/release until a dedicated replacement includes writers AND readers. Local materialization retains windowed CAS/verification/reclamation/holds. Session/login/profile/JWKS stores retain confidentiality/enumeration, exclusive .consumed-before-delete, merge/readback or expiry/issuer/key laws. Local placement/recovery artifacts, credential/crypto staging and Git-backed roadmap_event_carrier do not move merely because slot metadata does."),
    p(text: "**Validate:** start with only parent directory; provision/read/use as consumer principal; repeated setup is Noop, duplicate claim retains refusal. Remove prerequisite production, deny access, supply wrong instance/foreign owner, prevent readback or inject unresolved put/cleanup residue: complete success must stop before launch. Preserve distinct lost race, unreadable enumeration, missing/corrupt object, unknown publication and crash-gap outcomes. Both selected backends execute their admitted object route with example-standing receipts; claims run on each backend admitted for their WHOLE contract. Keep real Git/file/provider routes beside supplied controls and isolate intentional corrupt/missing-object fixtures. Extend checkpoint plan-binding/unknown-put controls, protected-state/wire and writer-identity witnesses; do not keep obsolete directory enrollment merely to satisfy old tests."),
    p(text: "**Completion/open decisions:** no surviving consumer left bound to the retired authority (the zero-undispositioned census is retired by the 2026-10-30 process ruling (`gunbc.design_ruling bad_process_is_worse_than_no_process`)); one executing authority, no fallback/flags, reconciled subject identities and accounted evidence under replacement-migration-doctrine. Ordinary snapshot/claim callers stay unchanged in a second isolated deployment; necessary root bindings are named/justified. Still decide existing fabric policy placement, full recovery enumeration/retention, R2 composed operations and the next bounded compiler derivation. Generic effect protocol/goal revision stay with fleet; #14757 is only a domain example. Expect real serialization/network/credential overhead, stronger readiness refusals and preserved custody; supplied 0/0 does not estimate execution. Later calibrated inputs refine the same receipt/interface without changing consumers."),
  ]
}

data logical_work_realization_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "logical-work-realization",
  title: "Logical work realization: a small SLO and arbitration interface",
  body: logical_work_realization_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Retire this proposal when fabric-owned selection executes both file and R2 backends through the shared storage interface with explicit example-standing controls, recording and settlement consume the same grounded fabric binding, feature callers no longer author infrastructure arguments or independent setup enrollment, both provisioning routes consume the same requirements, and the unchanged logical caller works in a second isolated deployment. The owning domain models must carry the policy, selection-to-effect connection and executed controls. Any remaining authored root binding is named and justified. Production metering is a refinement of those inputs, not a retirement prerequisite; remaining general compiler-completion obligations are recorded in the existing implementation program. Those consumed contracts and evidence then own the facts this proposal discusses.") },
}
